From 1a9606f688211bf77d3f2811a90bb572688878d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:50:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] Transform feedback queries

VK_QUERY_TYPE_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM_EXT was not supported (vkCreateQueryPool failed, Begin/EndQueryIndexedEXT
were no-ops) and transformFeedbackQueries was false: vkd3d-proton refuses to create a D3D12 device without it,
DXVK's D3D11 stream-output statistics queries failed.

- MVKTransformFeedbackQueryPool: 2 uint64 results per query (primitives written, primitives needed) in a shared
  MTLBuffer, reset on the GPU (vkCmdResetQueryPool) or the host (vkResetQueryPool).
- The query active for vertex stream 0 is tracked by the encoder. The compute pass that turns a capturing
  geometry-shader draw's per-primitive vertex counts into vertex slots adds the vertices written and the vertices
  counted, divided by the vertices of the geometry shader's output primitive (points 1, line strips 2, triangle
  strips 3), to the query's results. Draws without transform feedback active, without a capturing geometry
  shader, or indirect (not captured) count nothing.
- vkCmdBeginQueryIndexedEXT / vkCmdEndQueryIndexedEXT record Begin/EndQuery. Only stream 0 exists
  (maxTransformFeedbackStreams 1); queries of other streams (vkd3d-proton and DXVK use the D3D stream index)
  are not begun and end with their reset value 0.
- vkGetQueryPoolResults and the vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults kernel write every result of a query (was only the
  first), followed by the availability value.
- transformFeedbackQueries = true.
